WEBVTT

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:36.828
Fourscore and 1,145 years ago,

00:00:36.912 --> 00:00:40.832
our forefathers' foreheads
conceived a new nation.

00:00:40.958 --> 00:00:44.169
And this Presidents' Day,
we honoreth those values

00:00:44.253 --> 00:00:46.421
that my body fought and died for.

00:00:46.672 --> 00:00:49.633
Values like this brand-new Plymouth Vager.

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:52.052
Hi, I'm Malfunctioning Eddie,

00:00:52.135 --> 00:00:54.054
and I'm malfunctioning so badly,

00:00:54.137 --> 00:00:56.723
I'm practically giving these cars away.

00:00:56.807 --> 00:00:59.184
Hey, let's go car shopping.

00:00:59.268 --> 00:01:02.479
My parents promised if I got all B's,
they'd buy me a bar,

00:01:02.563 --> 00:01:03.939
and I got all C's.

00:01:04.022 --> 00:01:05.440
Mind if I tag along?

00:01:05.524 --> 00:01:07.901
I've got to bring my ass in for servicing.

00:01:08.026 --> 00:01:11.613
The recall notice says it could burst
into flame in a low-speed collision.

00:01:11.697 --> 00:01:14.700
No wonder you've been staying
at the back of conga lines lately.

00:01:14.783 --> 00:01:16.034
I'll get my coat.

00:01:16.118 --> 00:01:17.286
Let's go, Bender.

00:01:23.542 --> 00:01:25.711
Hello. I am Victor,

00:01:25.794 --> 00:01:28.130
and I know many things
about the art of unloading

00:01:28.213 --> 00:01:30.799
fine cars on beautiful women.

00:01:31.216 --> 00:01:32.259
Uh-huh...

00:01:32.342 --> 00:01:34.344
Now tell her she's witty
and sophisticated.

00:01:34.511 --> 00:01:38.849
Ah, ah, ah. A gentlemen always
sells a lady a car first.

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:41.101
This is the Beta Romeo.

00:01:41.185 --> 00:01:43.395
Yes, the Beta Romeo.

00:01:43.478 --> 00:01:45.814
Note the cross-your-heart seat belt

00:01:45.898 --> 00:01:49.026
which protects, lifts and separates.

00:01:53.238 --> 00:01:55.949
Spotted her the minute
you walked in, didn't you, sir?

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:57.034
She's a real beauty.

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:59.328
Yeah, she's beautiful coffee all right.

00:01:59.411 --> 00:02:01.788
No, the Ford Thunder-Cougar-Falcon-bird.

00:02:02.289 --> 00:02:03.999
Nothing makes you feel more like a man

00:02:04.082 --> 00:02:05.667
than a Thunder-Cougar-Falcon-bird.

00:02:05.751 --> 00:02:08.128
So, how much were you thinking
of spending on this?

00:02:08.212 --> 00:02:09.671
Sorry. I'm not here to buy.

00:02:09.755 --> 00:02:11.798
I understand.
It's wonderful that you don't care

00:02:11.882 --> 00:02:14.176
whether anyone questions
your sexual orientation.

00:02:14.259 --> 00:02:17.471
I care. I care plenty!
I just don't know how to make them stop.

00:02:17.554 --> 00:02:18.555
One word...

00:02:18.639 --> 00:02:19.973
Thunder-Cougar-Falcon-bird.

00:02:20.057 --> 00:02:23.352
The luxurious seats
are stuffed with eagle down.

00:02:23.435 --> 00:02:27.356
And the dashboard inlaid
with the beaks of a thousand eagles.

00:02:27.439 --> 00:02:30.776
Also, there are some eagles
under the floorboards.

00:02:30.859 --> 00:02:32.402
That's an awful lot of eagle.

00:02:32.486 --> 00:02:34.613
Yes, and yet...

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:37.241
What's wrong?

00:02:37.324 --> 00:02:41.328
It is just that the luxury edition
has so much more eagle.

00:02:41.411 --> 00:02:43.914
It saddens me to think of you missing out.

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:45.958
Oh, don't be sad.

00:02:46.041 --> 00:02:48.752
My parents are paying
and they're incredibly rich.

00:02:53.465 --> 00:02:55.843
Ow... Ow...

00:03:00.514 --> 00:03:02.307
I installed shock-absorbing bumpers

00:03:02.391 --> 00:03:04.476
to reduce the risk
of catastrophic butt failure.

00:03:05.477 --> 00:03:09.064
You, sir, have defaced
a national treasure.

00:03:09.147 --> 00:03:11.275
I demand you restore my buttocks

00:03:11.358 --> 00:03:13.944
to their former glory!

00:03:14.236 --> 00:03:18.282
All right, but sooner or later
that ass is going to blow,

00:03:18.365 --> 00:03:20.868
and when it does, I just pray

00:03:20.951 --> 00:03:23.787
you're not mooning someone you care about.

00:03:23.871 --> 00:03:25.497
Smeesh, Leela,

00:03:25.581 --> 00:03:28.625
this car has everything
a beautiful woman like me needs.

00:03:28.709 --> 00:03:30.169
Victor said so.

00:03:30.252 --> 00:03:33.922
No dog food for Victor tonight.

00:03:34.631 --> 00:03:37.342
Okay. The sticker says 55,000,

00:03:37.426 --> 00:03:39.845
but we'll only go as high as, say...

00:03:39.928 --> 00:03:40.929
Sixty thousand!

00:03:41.096 --> 00:03:42.472
Oh...

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:44.933
I will have to ask my manager.

00:03:45.559 --> 00:03:48.645
Amy, you don't go up
from the sticker price.

00:03:48.729 --> 00:03:50.355
I thought it was an auction.

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:55.986
He is not too happy.

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:57.112
I'm sorry.

00:03:57.196 --> 00:03:58.322
Eighty thousand?

00:04:04.203 --> 00:04:05.204
Uh-oh.

00:04:05.287 --> 00:04:07.206
I'm terrible at parallel parking.

00:04:11.168 --> 00:04:13.420
And now you're asking
for a day off?

00:04:13.504 --> 00:04:15.214
Get out of my and my sight.

00:04:15.297 --> 00:04:16.924
You're bogarting my patience.

00:04:18.133 --> 00:04:19.885
Hermes, who were you yelling at?

00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:22.804
Meself. I asked meself
for Valentine's Day off,

00:04:22.888 --> 00:04:25.641
but I was in no mood
for any of my shenanigans.

00:04:25.724 --> 00:04:27.434
Valentine's Day is coming?

00:04:27.518 --> 00:04:28.769
Oh, crap.

00:04:28.852 --> 00:04:30.562
I forgot to get a girlfriend again.

00:04:30.646 --> 00:04:33.023
Well, since neither of us has a date,
why don't we...

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:35.651
You just assume
I can't get a Valentine's date?

00:04:36.485 --> 00:04:37.861
Shall we say 8:00?

00:04:37.945 --> 00:04:40.948
Hey, I'm taking my new car out
for a spin to Mercury.

00:04:41.031 --> 00:04:43.659
- Anybody want to come?
- Yeah, okay. What's the weather like?

00:04:43.742 --> 00:04:46.495
The usual. Boiling lead, oceans of lava.

00:04:46.578 --> 00:04:48.330
So, what? Shorts?

00:04:58.465 --> 00:05:00.634
Boy, this AC is incredible.

00:05:02.219 --> 00:05:03.679
I'd better turn on the heater, too.

00:05:12.813 --> 00:05:14.773
Boy, this heater is incredible.

00:05:14.857 --> 00:05:16.608
I'd better turn up the AC some more.

00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:21.071
Hey, how about some icy margaritas?

00:05:21.154 --> 00:05:22.281
Yeah.

00:05:28.287 --> 00:05:29.705
We're slowing down.

00:05:29.788 --> 00:05:32.416
Don't worry, I'll hit the fuel guzzler.

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:36.378
Who wants Pop-Tarts?

00:05:46.346 --> 00:05:47.347
Oh!

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:50.851
Uh-oh.

00:05:50.934 --> 00:05:52.978
It's okay. I have an emergency phone.

00:05:58.358 --> 00:05:59.568
What are you doing?

00:05:59.651 --> 00:06:01.778
Spluh, it's a video-phone.

00:06:03.530 --> 00:06:07.618
Lucky I'm a member of the Austro-Afro
Antarctico-Amerasian Auto Association.

00:06:07.701 --> 00:06:09.161
Hello? Septuple-A?

00:06:14.917 --> 00:06:15.918
Phew!

00:06:17.336 --> 00:06:19.046
Oh, it'll be a couple hours.

00:06:19.671 --> 00:06:22.633
Oh! I'm going to get sweat
on my sweat suit.

00:06:23.759 --> 00:06:25.427
Hey, tell me something.

00:06:25.511 --> 00:06:26.637
You've got all this money,

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:28.889
how come you always dress
like you're doing your laundry?

00:06:28.972 --> 00:06:31.725
I guess 'cause my parents keep
telling me to be more ladylike.

00:06:31.808 --> 00:06:32.851
As though.

00:06:32.935 --> 00:06:34.144
I've been there.

00:06:34.228 --> 00:06:35.979
My folks were always on me to groom myself

00:06:36.063 --> 00:06:37.064
and wear underpants.

00:06:37.147 --> 00:06:38.190
What am I, the Pope?

00:06:38.315 --> 00:06:40.609
Yeah. And if you were the Pope

00:06:40.692 --> 00:06:42.694
they'd be all, "Straighten your pope hat,"

00:06:42.778 --> 00:06:44.613
and "Put on your good vestments."

00:06:47.950 --> 00:06:49.034
You know, Fry,

00:06:49.117 --> 00:06:52.496
it's nice to find someone
I can talk to about stuff and junk.

00:06:52.579 --> 00:06:56.083
Yeah, it's like we feel
the same way about junk and stuff,

00:06:56.166 --> 00:06:57.376
or whatever.

00:07:10.389 --> 00:07:11.557
Oh, ho!

00:07:17.563 --> 00:07:18.730
So while they're towing us,

00:07:18.814 --> 00:07:20.107
- you want to do it?
- Yeah!

00:07:22.067 --> 00:07:24.069
Yo, ho, ho, ho, ho!

00:07:28.699 --> 00:07:31.660
Which concludes the summary
of the movie I saw last night.

00:07:31.743 --> 00:07:33.579
Now, any old business?

00:07:33.662 --> 00:07:35.664
- No.
- Any new business?

00:07:35.747 --> 00:07:36.748
No.

00:07:36.832 --> 00:07:38.417
Anyone spend the night together?

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:39.501
- No.
- Yep.

00:07:39.585 --> 00:07:41.295
Kind of.

00:07:41.461 --> 00:07:44.256
- What?
- Oh, my God!

00:07:44.339 --> 00:07:47.467
We ran out of fuel on Mercury
and one thing led to another.

00:07:47.551 --> 00:07:49.595
And it led there again when we got home.

00:07:53.432 --> 00:07:54.808
Congratulations, Fry.

00:07:54.892 --> 00:07:56.727
You snagged the perfect girlfriend.

00:07:56.810 --> 00:07:57.895
Amy is rich.

00:07:57.978 --> 00:08:00.439
She's probably got other characteristics.

00:08:00.522 --> 00:08:02.983
Bender! Romance isn't about money.

00:08:03.066 --> 00:08:05.110
Oh, so it's just coincidence

00:08:05.194 --> 00:08:07.154
that Zoidberg here is desperately poor

00:08:07.237 --> 00:08:08.780
and miserably lonely?

00:08:08.864 --> 00:08:09.907
Please.

00:08:09.990 --> 00:08:13.076
For your information,
it's because he's hideous.

00:08:14.703 --> 00:08:17.998
Well, I think Fry and Amy go together
like a lime and a coconut.

00:08:18.081 --> 00:08:20.292
Do I hear wedding bells?

00:08:20.375 --> 00:08:21.585
What? No!

00:08:21.668 --> 00:08:23.921
Really? Oh, dear.

00:08:24.046 --> 00:08:26.632
Oh... You're both very lucky.

00:08:26.715 --> 00:08:30.260
I'd pay anything to end
my miserable loneliness,

00:08:30.344 --> 00:08:33.013
if only I weren't so desperately poor.

00:08:33.096 --> 00:08:36.350
Wait. You mean people
will pay good money for romance?

00:08:36.475 --> 00:08:40.229
Hmm, I think I have a scheme
so deviously clever that I...

00:08:40.812 --> 00:08:42.731
Five hundred dollars and time served.

00:08:42.814 --> 00:08:44.900
Stupid anti-pimping laws.

00:08:44.983 --> 00:08:46.693
Well, pay the man.

00:08:47.486 --> 00:08:49.029
Bender, honey, we love you.

00:08:49.112 --> 00:08:50.656
Sure, baby, I know it.

00:08:54.952 --> 00:08:56.870
Ah! Computer dating.

00:08:56.954 --> 00:09:00.666
It's like pimping, but you rarely
have to use the phrase "Upside your head."

00:09:00.749 --> 00:09:02.209
Bender, this is stupid.

00:09:02.292 --> 00:09:04.670
Why would anyone come to you
for romantic help?

00:09:04.753 --> 00:09:06.797
Hey! Don't make me go upside your head!

00:09:09.007 --> 00:09:10.467
Fry! Amy!

00:09:10.551 --> 00:09:13.887
Put your pants back on!
I need a stapler!

00:09:14.096 --> 00:09:15.305
Stop. Stop!

00:09:15.389 --> 00:09:18.600
If you interrupt the mating dance,
the male will become enraged

00:09:18.684 --> 00:09:21.019
and maul us with his fearsome gonad.

00:09:21.103 --> 00:09:23.272
It's working. They think we're making out.

00:09:25.858 --> 00:09:27.651
Wait. Why aren't we making out?

00:09:27.734 --> 00:09:28.735
I don't know.

00:09:32.114 --> 00:09:33.782
Okay, mister...

00:09:33.866 --> 00:09:34.867
Smith.

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:36.660
Zapp Smith. Brannigan.

00:09:36.743 --> 00:09:39.538
Just check off the things
you're looking for in a love partner.

00:09:39.621 --> 00:09:41.081
Let's see.

00:09:41.164 --> 00:09:42.165
Oh, yes.

00:09:42.499 --> 00:09:44.001
Yes, definitely.

00:09:44.418 --> 00:09:45.919
Mmm, I'd like some of that.

00:09:46.211 --> 00:09:49.923
Mmm! I'll just have everything
on the menu.

00:09:50.841 --> 00:09:54.970
Now, to run it through
our high-speed romance-alogical datafier.

00:10:00.934 --> 00:10:01.935
Beep.

00:10:02.311 --> 00:10:04.396
Say hello to Miss Right.

00:10:04.479 --> 00:10:05.564
Hello.

00:10:10.027 --> 00:10:11.028
Wow.

00:10:11.111 --> 00:10:12.321
We're great kissers.

00:10:12.696 --> 00:10:13.697
Yeah.

00:10:13.780 --> 00:10:16.283
Hey, later, you want
to drive out to Europa?

00:10:16.366 --> 00:10:18.869
We could have a picnic
and spit watermelon seeds at Jupiter.

00:10:18.952 --> 00:10:22.247
Hey, yeah. I used to spit at stuff
back in the 20th century.

00:10:22.915 --> 00:10:25.501
Ah, it's cool how we
sort of think exactly alike,

00:10:25.584 --> 00:10:26.919
- and junk.
- Yeah.

00:10:27.002 --> 00:10:29.296
You know, Fry, I really like
hanging out with you.

00:10:32.007 --> 00:10:33.175
Everything was going great.

00:10:33.258 --> 00:10:35.928
Then all of a sudden,
she's talking about hanging out.

00:10:36.053 --> 00:10:37.804
"Hanging out"?

00:10:37.888 --> 00:10:39.556
She's getting way too serious.

00:10:39.765 --> 00:10:41.308
I'm not a one-woman man, Leela.

00:10:41.391 --> 00:10:43.477
You'll be back to zero soon enough.

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:45.646
Don't you get it? She's smothering me.

00:10:45.729 --> 00:10:47.356
- Hi.
- You see? You see?

00:10:47.439 --> 00:10:49.191
Now she's bothering me when I'm at work.

00:10:49.274 --> 00:10:51.860
- Fry.
- I'm doing my job... There's Amy.

00:10:51.944 --> 00:10:55.072
I spend a few hours selecting
a candy from the machine... There's Amy.

00:10:55.155 --> 00:10:57.115
I wake up the morning
after sleeping with Amy...

00:10:57.199 --> 00:10:59.493
- There's Amy.
- I think you're overreacting.

00:10:59.576 --> 00:11:00.577
Am I?

00:11:00.661 --> 00:11:01.662
Am I!

00:11:01.745 --> 00:11:03.830
Face it. I'm a prize catch.

00:11:04.122 --> 00:11:06.583
I mean, I'm pulling down
delivery-boy money.

00:11:06.959 --> 00:11:09.711
Fry, she's pulling down
billionaire trust-fund money.

00:11:09.795 --> 00:11:11.588
Then she wants me as a trophy husband.

00:11:11.672 --> 00:11:13.882
Leela, you gotta come to Europa with us.

00:11:13.966 --> 00:11:15.384
I can't be alone with her.

00:11:15.676 --> 00:11:18.303
So, ready for a secluded picnic
with just you and me?

00:11:18.387 --> 00:11:21.473
Hey, you know who loves
secluded picnics with just you and me?

00:11:22.599 --> 00:11:23.600
Uh...

00:11:23.767 --> 00:11:24.768
Dr. Zoidberg.

00:11:25.853 --> 00:11:29.147
Did someone say something
about a free hot meal?

00:11:39.116 --> 00:11:41.410
Mmm, I haven't eaten since Tuesday.

00:11:41.702 --> 00:11:43.996
Bird eggs, animal slices,

00:11:45.205 --> 00:11:46.832
dry woven reeds.

00:11:48.917 --> 00:11:49.918
All gone.

00:11:50.002 --> 00:11:51.545
- Can I drive?
- No.

00:11:51.628 --> 00:11:53.380
So, Fry, you busy tomorrow?

00:11:53.463 --> 00:11:55.174
I got two tickets to the big ape fight.

00:11:55.257 --> 00:11:58.385
Geez, we're already planning
to spend Valentine's Day together.

00:11:58.468 --> 00:12:00.804
- Isn't that enough?
- Okay. Sure.

00:12:01.346 --> 00:12:03.015
What do you want to do
for Valentine's Day?

00:12:03.098 --> 00:12:05.726
Oh, so all of a sudden
we're spending Valentine's Day together?

00:12:05.809 --> 00:12:08.270
- But you just said...
- That's it, Amy, we have to talk.

00:12:08.353 --> 00:12:09.521
Zoidberg, you drive.

00:12:09.688 --> 00:12:10.689
Wahoo.

00:12:11.231 --> 00:12:12.691
Pardon me. Excuse me.

00:12:13.525 --> 00:12:17.070
Ah, I'll just turn the wheel
to maximum fastness.

00:12:18.238 --> 00:12:20.699
Amy, you know how,
at first, you like chocolate

00:12:20.782 --> 00:12:22.326
but then you start to get tired of it

00:12:22.409 --> 00:12:24.036
'cause it always wants
to hang out with you?

00:12:24.161 --> 00:12:27.706
- Huh? You don't like chocolate?
- Look, could chocolate just let me finish?

00:12:27.956 --> 00:12:29.416
Vroom, vroom.

00:12:29.499 --> 00:12:32.127
And the winner of the big car race is

00:12:32.211 --> 00:12:34.671
hot rod Zoidberg!

00:12:36.548 --> 00:12:38.342
Amy, what I'm trying to say is,

00:12:38.425 --> 00:12:40.427
I think, maybe you and I should stop...

00:12:40.552 --> 00:12:41.845
Uh-oh.

00:12:42.095 --> 00:12:43.222
Here, you drive.

00:12:55.150 --> 00:12:57.194
Fry, are you all right?

00:12:58.904 --> 00:13:00.572
My head is killing me.

00:13:01.073 --> 00:13:02.908
What happened? Was anybody hurt?

00:13:02.991 --> 00:13:04.076
No, no, no, no, no.

00:13:04.159 --> 00:13:05.327
Of course not.

00:13:05.410 --> 00:13:06.787
Nobody but you.

00:13:06.870 --> 00:13:10.040
I'm afraid your body
was badly damaged in the crash.

00:13:10.123 --> 00:13:12.459
- How badly?
- That's it over there.

00:13:13.961 --> 00:13:15.879
Don't worry.

00:13:15.963 --> 00:13:19.091
I managed to keep your head alive
with some quick surgery.

00:13:19.174 --> 00:13:21.218
- Where is it?
- There.

00:13:21.969 --> 00:13:24.888
Looks like we'll be spending
a lot more time together, Fry.

00:13:31.311 --> 00:13:34.064
This sort of thing always happens

00:13:34.147 --> 00:13:35.566
with office romances.

00:13:35.649 --> 00:13:36.775
Don't worry, Fry,

00:13:36.859 --> 00:13:39.820
we'll have your body
all fixed up in a few days.

00:13:40.153 --> 00:13:41.321
Oops-a-daisy.

00:13:44.199 --> 00:13:46.952
Well, Amy, I'll try not to interfere
with your life too much.

00:13:47.411 --> 00:13:49.246
- Fry!
- Oh, sorry.

00:13:49.329 --> 00:13:50.914
I guess I control that arm.

00:13:53.458 --> 00:13:56.461
So, what was it you wanted to talk about
before we crashed, anyway?

00:13:56.545 --> 00:13:57.838
Oh, that.

00:13:57.921 --> 00:13:59.631
Maybe we'd better talk in private.

00:14:00.132 --> 00:14:01.675
I'll meet you in the closet.

00:14:02.551 --> 00:14:03.969
Amy, I really like you

00:14:04.052 --> 00:14:05.262
as a friend,

00:14:05.345 --> 00:14:07.556
but I think we're spending
too much time together.

00:14:07.639 --> 00:14:09.141
You're breaking up with me?

00:14:09.224 --> 00:14:11.435
I just think we should
start seeing other people.

00:14:11.518 --> 00:14:13.770
But, I was really having fun.

00:14:14.938 --> 00:14:16.231
If that's how you feel...

00:14:16.315 --> 00:14:17.983
I'm sorry, but it is.

00:14:18.734 --> 00:14:19.985
Well, whatever.

00:14:20.068 --> 00:14:22.196
Hey, listen, as long as
we're not seeing each other,

00:14:22.279 --> 00:14:24.448
you mind if I ask
someone else out for Valentine's Day?

00:14:24.948 --> 00:14:27.743
I mean, unless it'd make you
feel bad being a third wheel.

00:14:27.826 --> 00:14:29.620
Hey, I can get a date, too.

00:14:29.953 --> 00:14:32.414
Now that I'm single
I'll attract all sorts of women.

00:14:32.497 --> 00:14:33.582
With my body,

00:14:33.665 --> 00:14:36.210
I think you might only attract
one sort of woman.

00:14:36.293 --> 00:14:37.294
Oh!

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:38.921
Oh.

00:14:43.383 --> 00:14:44.384
So...

00:14:44.468 --> 00:14:45.469
How's business?

00:14:47.471 --> 00:14:50.390
Are you familiar with my friend Al Gore?

00:14:50.474 --> 00:14:51.558
I'm telling you,

00:14:51.642 --> 00:14:54.353
losers get really desperate
around Valentine's Day.

00:14:54.436 --> 00:14:56.772
Yeah. It's pathetic, all right.

00:15:01.944 --> 00:15:03.320
- How much?
- Five hundred bucks.

00:15:03.403 --> 00:15:05.322
- Done.
- Zapp Brannigan okay?

00:15:05.405 --> 00:15:06.532
- No.
- Six hundred.

00:15:15.916 --> 00:15:16.959
Oh, hey, Leela.

00:15:17.251 --> 00:15:18.293
Can I talk to you for a minute,

00:15:18.794 --> 00:15:19.837
in private?

00:15:19.962 --> 00:15:21.672
Oh. No problem.

00:15:25.467 --> 00:15:26.718
This is an emergency.

00:15:26.802 --> 00:15:29.137
Amy made Valentine's plans with some goon

00:15:29.221 --> 00:15:31.765
and I'm going to be stuck there
lonely and miserable.

00:15:31.849 --> 00:15:33.350
Will you be my date?

00:15:33.433 --> 00:15:34.434
Please?

00:15:34.726 --> 00:15:35.894
You're too late, Fry.

00:15:35.978 --> 00:15:39.189
I'm sharing Valentine's Day
with a very special man.

00:15:39.273 --> 00:15:40.816
He's not Zapp Brannigan or anything.

00:15:40.899 --> 00:15:42.568
Then I have no choice but to do something

00:15:42.651 --> 00:15:45.404
so pitiful and embarrassing
that I'm ashamed to tell you about it.

00:15:45.487 --> 00:15:47.114
- Bender is in his office.
- Thanks.

00:15:50.450 --> 00:15:52.160
I got your hookup, Fry.

00:15:52.244 --> 00:15:54.329
Now, my usual fee is 500 bucks,

00:15:54.663 --> 00:15:56.164
but seeing as how it's you,

00:15:56.248 --> 00:15:57.749
I'll need it in advance.

00:16:00.794 --> 00:16:03.547
Okay, Fry, we're done putting on the bra.

00:16:03.630 --> 00:16:06.175
Why exactly did you
shave your legs, anyway?

00:16:06.258 --> 00:16:09.011
Are you expecting something to happen
with your Valentine's date?

00:16:09.094 --> 00:16:10.512
What business is it of yours?

00:16:10.596 --> 00:16:13.265
And another thing, you're using
an awful lot of makeup there.

00:16:13.348 --> 00:16:14.558
This is deodorant.

00:16:14.641 --> 00:16:16.476
What does it do?

00:16:16.643 --> 00:16:17.686
Come on in, Gary.

00:16:17.769 --> 00:16:19.563
I'll just be another 20 minutes.

00:16:20.272 --> 00:16:21.607
I'll be waiting.

00:16:22.191 --> 00:16:23.192
Twenty minutes?

00:16:23.275 --> 00:16:24.776
You're practically ready now.

00:16:24.860 --> 00:16:26.528
Yeah, but it's good
to make them wait a little.

00:16:26.612 --> 00:16:28.822
Oh, God, it's true!

00:16:35.746 --> 00:16:38.123
That dress looks great on you.

00:16:38.207 --> 00:16:39.208
- Thanks.
- Thanks.

00:16:39.291 --> 00:16:40.626
Where is she?

00:16:41.793 --> 00:16:44.004
I must say, Amy, you're all made up.

00:16:44.463 --> 00:16:45.964
Just like Fry's date.

00:16:46.048 --> 00:16:47.466
- Get it?
- Mmm-mmm.

00:16:47.925 --> 00:16:49.051
I've got a date!

00:16:49.134 --> 00:16:50.344
She'll be along any minute.

00:16:50.427 --> 00:16:52.221
Fry! Look who I found.

00:16:52.304 --> 00:16:55.641
It's Petunia! Your dream girl.

00:16:55.724 --> 00:16:56.975
- How's them eats?
- Uh...

00:16:57.059 --> 00:16:58.310
Don't mind if I do.

00:16:59.269 --> 00:17:00.270
Kids'll be hungry.

00:17:00.354 --> 00:17:02.189
She seems a little old for me.

00:17:02.272 --> 00:17:03.649
She is well-traveled,

00:17:03.732 --> 00:17:05.400
and I don't mean she travels a lot.

00:17:05.484 --> 00:17:07.027
Wheels fell off my house.

00:17:07.110 --> 00:17:08.904
Now, how about a rose for the lady?

00:17:08.987 --> 00:17:10.072
Five bucks a pop.

00:17:10.155 --> 00:17:11.448
- I'll take one.
- Oh, yeah?

00:17:11.532 --> 00:17:12.741
Well, I want one, too.

00:17:12.824 --> 00:17:14.284
- Eight bucks.
- But, you just said...

00:17:14.368 --> 00:17:15.953
Demand suddenly skyrocketed.

00:17:16.036 --> 00:17:17.162
You all saw it!

00:17:22.251 --> 00:17:25.128
Leela, meet your future husband, Sal.

00:17:25.337 --> 00:17:27.506
Eeh. Nice eyeball, eyeball.

00:17:27.589 --> 00:17:28.882
Nice ass, ass.

00:17:29.091 --> 00:17:31.385
Ooh, sparks. Buy her a rose,

00:17:31.468 --> 00:17:32.719
I guarantee she'll put out.

00:17:34.179 --> 00:17:35.931
Eh, I'll take my chances.

00:17:40.811 --> 00:17:42.521
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

00:17:43.272 --> 00:17:44.857
So, tell me about your prospects.

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:46.650
- You a good gambler?
- Well, ma'am, I...

00:17:46.733 --> 00:17:48.277
What's your game? Bingo?

00:17:48.360 --> 00:17:50.279
Keno? Wait a minute.

00:17:50.362 --> 00:17:51.405
You don't have your own body.

00:17:51.488 --> 00:17:53.115
No, but I control this arm.

00:17:53.198 --> 00:17:54.366
Slots player, huh?

00:17:55.033 --> 00:17:56.743
Sorry, but I think I can do better.

00:17:56.827 --> 00:17:58.245
Wait! Come back...

00:17:58.328 --> 00:17:59.913
- darling.
- Can't, hon.

00:17:59.997 --> 00:18:01.874
I got to catch my bus back to Nutley.

00:18:01.957 --> 00:18:05.085
I'd kiss you good night,
but I lost my teeth pulling out a stump.

00:18:05.377 --> 00:18:06.503
So, anyways, Leela,

00:18:06.587 --> 00:18:08.380
I'd love to take a whack at you,

00:18:08.463 --> 00:18:10.883
but that 10:15 to Nutley
ain't going nowheres

00:18:10.966 --> 00:18:12.968
without yours truly behind the wheel.

00:18:13.051 --> 00:18:14.136
Excuse me.

00:18:14.219 --> 00:18:17.222
Did you say, "10:15 to Nutley"?

00:18:17.306 --> 00:18:19.349
Why, yes, I did.

00:18:28.317 --> 00:18:31.987
Bender, did you just round up
our dates at the bus station?

00:18:32.070 --> 00:18:34.823
- Of course not.
- Anybody's else for Nutley?

00:18:37.701 --> 00:18:38.702
Baby, wait.

00:18:38.785 --> 00:18:40.746
You didn't show me your surprise.

00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:44.917
You know
what I'd like to do is...

00:18:45.292 --> 00:18:47.336
Oh, geez, get a room.

00:18:47.669 --> 00:18:48.670
Maybe later.

00:18:50.130 --> 00:18:53.717
Hey, I have an idea.
Let's all go out for ice cream.

00:18:53.800 --> 00:18:55.802
Actually, I thought Amy might like

00:18:55.886 --> 00:18:57.596
to come back to my place for coffee.

00:18:57.679 --> 00:18:59.056
I don't really like coffee.

00:18:59.139 --> 00:19:00.140
Neither do I.

00:19:01.767 --> 00:19:04.061
Ooh... I feel a little tipsy.

00:19:05.354 --> 00:19:07.022
Let me pick up the check.

00:19:10.859 --> 00:19:12.486
No!

00:19:19.576 --> 00:19:21.620
That's it! I'm getting
the hell out of here!

00:19:30.045 --> 00:19:33.048
Why, if it isn't my favorite head
on Amy's body,

00:19:33.131 --> 00:19:34.132
- Fry.
- Oh!

00:19:34.466 --> 00:19:36.885
- Leela!
- We were just on our way out.

00:19:36.969 --> 00:19:38.095
Nonsense.

00:19:38.178 --> 00:19:39.596
The evening is young.

00:19:39.680 --> 00:19:42.182
So, Gary, what do you do for a living?

00:19:42.266 --> 00:19:44.560
I'm a banking industry regulator.

00:19:44.685 --> 00:19:46.311
- Ugh!
- Really?

00:19:46.395 --> 00:19:49.314
You know, I heard
that banking industry regulations

00:19:49.398 --> 00:19:50.941
are really very simple.

00:19:51.024 --> 00:19:52.568
Oh, no, that's not true.

00:19:52.651 --> 00:19:54.945
You see, modern banking regulations

00:19:55.028 --> 00:19:58.574
are a product
of five different regulatory traditions.

00:19:58.907 --> 00:20:00.367
Six, if you want to get technical.

00:20:00.450 --> 00:20:01.660
Oh, I do.

00:20:02.369 --> 00:20:04.830
It all began in 1410,

00:20:04.913 --> 00:20:07.249
when a number of noblemen convened...

00:20:07.332 --> 00:20:08.667
Thank you.

00:20:12.004 --> 00:20:13.005
There you are.

00:20:13.088 --> 00:20:14.089
Good as new,

00:20:14.173 --> 00:20:15.632
except for your dorsal fin.

00:20:15.716 --> 00:20:18.427
I'm afraid I couldn't find it
after the crash.

00:20:18.510 --> 00:20:20.846
- Can I live without it?
- If you call that living.

00:20:20.929 --> 00:20:23.557
I still don't understand
why you wouldn't let me

00:20:23.640 --> 00:20:25.934
graft a laser cannon onto your chest

00:20:26.018 --> 00:20:28.520
to crush those who disobey you.

00:20:29.771 --> 00:20:32.774
Oh, but I guess,
we're just two different people.

00:20:33.483 --> 00:20:35.277
So, thanks for the ride, Amy,

00:20:35.360 --> 00:20:37.029
and I hope there are no hard feelings

00:20:37.112 --> 00:20:38.780
about your date, or stuff.

00:20:38.864 --> 00:20:40.532
It's okay. I had fun.

00:20:40.616 --> 00:20:41.950
And if I ever feel lonely,

00:20:42.034 --> 00:20:45.162
I can just look over
at this disfiguring scar and think of you.

00:20:49.416 --> 00:20:52.085
Well, anyway, it's nice
to have my own body back.

00:20:52.503 --> 00:20:53.629
Ah!

00:20:56.215 --> 00:20:57.216
Oh...

00:20:57.758 --> 00:20:59.218
So, how's the old corpse?

00:20:59.301 --> 00:21:00.719
Everything hooked up okay?

00:21:00.802 --> 00:21:03.055
Seems to be.
My neck is just a little tender.

00:21:03.430 --> 00:21:05.349
Ow! Cool.

00:21:05.766 --> 00:21:06.767
Ow!

00:21:06.850 --> 00:21:08.060
Listen, Leela,

00:21:08.143 --> 00:21:09.728
thanks for rescuing me last night.

00:21:09.811 --> 00:21:10.854
Anytime.

00:21:10.938 --> 00:21:12.940
I actually enjoyed hanging out with you.

00:21:13.023 --> 00:21:14.858
Yep. Everything worked out great.

00:21:14.942 --> 00:21:16.568
Thanks to good old Bender.

00:21:16.652 --> 00:21:17.653
Come on!

00:21:17.736 --> 00:21:20.531
It's not like you intentionally
set us up with bad dates

00:21:20.614 --> 00:21:22.574
so we'd spend Valentine's Day together.

00:21:22.658 --> 00:21:24.159
Didn't I, Leela?

00:21:24.243 --> 00:21:25.369
Didn't I?

00:21:26.703 --> 00:21:28.539
No! You didn't!

00:21:28.789 --> 00:21:31.208
You just corralled a bunch
of stiffs at the bus station

00:21:31.291 --> 00:21:32.376
and pocketed our money.

00:21:32.459 --> 00:21:34.461
True, but in the end,

00:21:34.545 --> 00:21:37.923
isn't that what Valentine's Day
is really all about?

00:21:38.006 --> 00:21:39.550
- Yeah.
- I guess so.

00:21:42.594 --> 00:21:44.388
Watch the neck. Watch the neck!

00:21:44.471 --> 00:21:45.514
My ass!

00:21:45.597 --> 00:21:46.807
My beautiful...